ammar" color="green">verb</font></div>to gain fame<ol><li><div>se faire connaître</div></li><li><div>se faire un nom</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div><div>faire parler de soi</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div><ol><li><div>mettre un point d'honneur à</div></li><li><div>se faire un point d'honneur de</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div><ol><li><div>faire des histoires</div></li><li><div>faire une scène</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div>To embarrass oneself or others in public<ol><li><div>se donner en spectacle</div></li><li><div>se faire remarquer</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div>To embarrass oneself or others in public<ol><li><div>s'offrir en spectacle</div></li><li><div>se couvrir de ridicule</div></li><li><div>se donner en spectacle</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div>to repair a relationship; to make up; to resolve an argument or fight; to make reparations or redress<ol><li><div>se réconcilier</div></li><li><div>donner satisfaction</div></li><li><div>faire amende honorable</div></li><li><div>obtenir satisfaction</div></li><li><div>se racheter</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div>turn up to an event<div>faire acte de présence</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div>to try; to work towards a goal<div>faire un effort</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div><div>faire son entrée</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div>punish someone as a warning to others<div>faire un exemple</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div>to embarrass oneself in public<div>se couvrir de ridicule</div></div><div><div><font class="