<div><font class="grammar" color="green">noun</font></div><ol><li>period of weather warm enough to melt ice, snow, etc.<div>dégel</div></li><li>gradual melting or softening of something frozen when the temperature rises<ol><li><div>dégel</div></li><li><div>fusion</div></li></ol></li><li>period of relaxation of restrictions in a country or state; period of increased friendliness or understanding, or of reduced hostility or tension in relations, between states<ol><li><div>dégel</div></li><li><div>réchauffement de l'atmosphère</div></li></ol></li></ol></div><div>/<font color="gray">θoː</font>/, /<font color="gray">θɑ</font>/, /<font color="gray">θɔ</font>/, /<font color="gray">θɔː</font>/<br>
<div><font class="grammar" color="green">verb</font></div><ol><li><ol><li><div>dégeler</div></li><li><div>fondre</div></li></ol></li><li>(transitive) to cause (someone or their feelings that are reserved or unfriendly) to become friendly or gentle; (intransitive) of a person or their feelings that are reserved or unfriendly: to become friendly or gentle<div>fondre</div></li></ol></div><div>/<font color="gray">jiː</font>/, /<font color="gray">ðeː</font>/, /<font color="gray">ði</font>/, /<font color="gray">ði/ [ðɪj]</font>/, /<font color="gray">ðiː</font>/, /<font color="gray">ðə</font>/, /<font color="gray">θeː</font>/<br>
<div><font class="grammar" color="green">adverb</font></div>the + comparative, the + comparative<div>le + comp., le + comp.</div></div><div>/<font color="gray">jiː</font>/, /<font color="gray">ðeː</font>/, /<font color="gray">ði</font>/, /<font color="gray">ði/ [ðɪj]</font>/, /<font color="gray">ðiː</font>/, /<font color="gray">ðə</font>/, /<font color="gray">θeː</font>/<br>
<div><font class="grammar" color="green">article</font></div><ol><li><ol><li>used with the name of a member of a class to refer to all things in that class</li><li>with a superlative</li><li>stressed, indicating that the object in question is the only one worthy of attention</li><li>used as an alternative to a possessive pronoun before body parts</li><li>introducing dates in a letter, such as "the 1st of May 2025"</li></ol><div>le</div></li><li>article<ol><li><div>le</div></li><li><div>la</div></li><li><div>les</div></li><li><div>l'</div></li></ol></li><li>with an adjectival noun, as in “the hungry” to mean “hungry people”<ol><li><div>les</div></li><li><div>le</div></li></ol></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>a child is similar to its parents<ol><li><div>les chiens ne font pas des chats</div></li><li><div>la pomme ne tombe jamais loin de l'arbre</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div><div>la balle est dans le camp de quelqu'un</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">noun</font></div>something excellent, outstanding<ol><li><div>c'est le must</div></li><li><div>le nec plus ultra</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>the most valuable things in life (e.g. friendship, courtesy) cost nothing<div>contentement passe richesse</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>the bill, please<div>l'addition, s'il vous plaît</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">noun</font></div><ol><li><div>arroseur arrosé</div></li><li><div>tel est pris qui croyait prendre</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>statement that no excuses will be made, that the speaker is going to take direct responsibility for matters, rather than pass the responsibility to higher authorities<ol><li><div>c'est ici que ça s'arrête</div></li><li><div>la responsabilité commence ici</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">pronoun</font></div>a former national anthem of South Africa<div>L'Appel de l'Afrique du Sud</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>a leader is ultimately responsible for the penalties of a catastrophe<div>le capitaine sombre avec son navire</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>The solution to a problem produces a worse net result<div>le remède est pire que le mal</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>proverb<ol><li><div>le client a toujours raison</div></li><li><div>le client est roi</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div><div>le mal est fait</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">adverb</font></div>on the preceding day<ol><li><div>la veille</div></li><li><div>le jour précédent</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>specific provisions of something may be complicated<div>le diable se cache dans les détails</div></div><div>/<font color="gray">ðə ˌdaɪ ɪz ˈkast</font>/, /<font color="gray">ðə ˌdaɪ ɪz ˈkæst</font>/, /<font color="gray">ðə ˌdaɪ ɪz ˈkɑːst</font>/<br>
<div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>a conclusive action has been taken, so events will proceed in an irreversible manner<ol><li><div>le sort en est jeté</div></li><li><div>alea jacta est</div></li><li><div>les dés sont jetés</div></li><li><div>les jeux sont faits</div></li><li><div>advienne que pourra</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>life goes on even if some will try to stop progress<ol><li><div>le chien aboie, la caravane passe</div></li><li><div>les chiens aboient, la caravane passe</div></li></ol></div><div>/<font color="gray">ði ˈɜɹli ˈbɜɹd ɡɛts ðə wɜɹm</font>/<br>
<div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>whoever arrives first has the best chance of success<ol><li><div>l'avenir appartient à ceux qui se lèvent tôt</div></li><li><div>la vache la première au pré, lèche toute la rosée</div></li><li><div>le monde appartient à ceux qui se lèvent tôt</div></li></ol></div><div>/<font color="gray">ði ɛnd</font>/, /<font color="gray">ðiː ɛnd</font>/<br>
<div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>end of a story or film<div>fin</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>morally wrong actions are sometimes necessary<ol><li><div>la fin justifie les moyens</div></li><li><div>qui veut la fin veut les moyens</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">noun</font></div>the point of having no more options<ol><li><div>au bout du rouleau</div></li><li><div>en dernier ressort</div></li><li><div>en désespoir de cause</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>it is sometimes necessary to cooperate with a person one does not like or agree with, in order to combat a common threat<div>l’ennemi de mon ennemi est mon ami</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div><div>il n'y a que le premier pas qui coûte</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>proverb<div>le poisson pourrit par la tête</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>one cannot change one's own nature<div>les loups peuvent perdre leurs dents, mais non le naturel</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div><ol><li>vulgar: intensifier forming part of a phrasal verb</li><li>vulgar: intensifier used after interrogative pronouns</li></ol><div>putain</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>Well-regarded people tend to die at a younger age<div>les meilleurs partent toujours les premiers</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>others' circumstances seem more desirable than one's own but in reality often are not.<ol><li><div>l'herbe est toujours plus verte ailleurs</div></li><li><div>l'herbe est toujours plus verte dans le pré du voisin</div></li></ol></div><div>/<font color="gray">ðə ˈheɪɡ</font>/, /<font color="gray">ðə ˈhæɡ</font>/<br>
<div><font class="grammar" color="green">pronoun</font></div>Dutch city<div>La Haye</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">adverb</font></div>by experiencing the consequences of making mistakes<div>à la dure</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">adverb</font></div>indication of emphatic rejection of an assertion<ol><li><div>mais bien sûr</div></li><li><div>que dalle</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">interjection</font></div>forget about it<div>au diable</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>a jug goes to the well<div>tant va la cruche à l'eau qu'à la fin elle se casse</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div><div>le roi est mort, vive le roi!</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>people deserve to be rewarded for their efforts<div>tout travail mérite salaire</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>because someone is insisting too much about something, the opposite must be true<div>la dame proteste un peu trop</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div><div>aux dernières nouvelles</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>the line is busy<ol><li><div>c'est occupé</div></li><li><div>la ligne est occupée</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">pronoun</font></div><ol><li>Christ or Messiah</li><li>king by divine right</li></ol><div>oint du Seigneur</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>it is more fun with more people<div>plus on est de fous, plus on rit</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>change is constant, unavoidable and a fact of life<div>plus ça change, plus c'est la même chose</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div><div>le clou qui dépasse se prend le marteau</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">adverb</font></div>the day that follows the one just spoken about<ol><li><div>le jour suivant</div></li><li><div>le lendemain</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>it's not very late<ol><li><div>la nuit ne fait que commencer</div></li><li><div>on a toute la nuit devant nous</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">noun</font></div>person destined to save the universe or world, also called the Chosen One<ol><li><div>l'élu</div></li><li><div>l'élue</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">pronoun</font></div>the person or thing<ol><li><div>celle</div></li><li><div>cellui</div></li><li><div>celui</div></li></ol></div><div>/<font color="gray">ði ˈɔɹɡən ˌɡɹaɪndəɹ nɑt ðə ˈmʌŋki</font>/, /<font color="gray">ðiː ˈɔːɡən ˌɡɹaɪndə nɒt ðə ˈmʌŋki</font>/<br>
<div><font class="grammar" color="green">noun</font></div>the organ grinder, not the monkey<div>il vaut mieux s’adresser au Bon Dieu qu’à ses saints</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">adverb</font></div>lately<ol><li><div>l'autre jour</div></li><li><div>ces derniers jours</div></li><li><div>dernièrement</div></li><li><div>récemment</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">adverb</font></div>same but with things reversed<ol><li><div>dans l'autre sens</div></li><li><div>vice versa</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>more power can be usurped by writing than fighting<div>la plume est plus forte que l’épée</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>understanding is reached, one comprehends<ol><li><div>faire tilt</div></li><li><div>la pièce est tombée</div></li><li><div>le franc est tombé</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>When you use a thing too much, it ultimately breaks<div>tant va la cruche à l'eau qu'à la fin elle se casse</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div><div>tout le plaisir est pour moi</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>used to describe an increasingly complex or mysterious situation<div>le mystère s'épaissit</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>the only real test of something is as what it is intended to be used for<ol><li><div>il faut juger sur pièces</div></li><li><div>la qualité se révèle à l’usage</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>Pangram<div>portez ce vieux whisky au juge blond qui fume</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>used to indicate that one does not need to continue a story<ol><li><div>le reste est de l'histoire</div></li><li><div>on connaît la suite</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>well-intended acts can lead to disasters<div>l'enfer est pavé de bonnes intentions</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">noun</font></div>something considered to be excellent<ol><li><div>de la balle</div></li><li><div>de la bombe</div></li><li><div>tuerie</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>one often neglects those closest to oneself<div>les cordonniers sont toujours les plus mal chaussés</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>One must finish what one has started.<div>le spectacle doit continuer</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>nothing is out of reach<div>rien n'est impossible</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>achieving something is made impossible by frailty<div>l'esprit est prompt, mais la chair est faible</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>the person who complains most receives the attention<div>ceux qui parlent le plus fort ont toute l'attention</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div><ol><li><div>il parait</div></li><li><div>on dit</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">noun</font></div>small additional burden which causes failure<div>la goutte d'eau qui fait déborder le vase</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>shift focus to an overriding point or impediment<div>le truc, c'est que</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div>the toilet is clogged<div>les toilettes sont bouchées</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>the voice of the people, the voice of God<div>la voix du peuple est la voix de Dieu</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div><ol><li><div>au train où vont les choses</div></li><li><div>si ça continue comme ça</div></li><li><div>à ce rythme-là</div></li></ol></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">noun</font></div>always<div>tout le temps</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">proverb</font></div>one cannot change one's own nature<div>chassez le naturel, il revient au galop</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">phraseologicalUnit</font></div><div>les carottes sont cuites</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">pronoun</font></div>a classical Greek mathematician<div>Théétète</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">pronoun</font></div><div>Théagène</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">noun</font></div><div>théalogie</div></div><div><div><font class="grammar" color="green">adjective</font></div>divine and human<div>théandrique</div></div><div>/<font color="gray">ˈθi(ə)tɚ</font>/, /<font color="gray">ˈθi.eɪ.tɚ</font>/, /<font color="gray">ˈθiətə</font>/, /<font color="gray">ˈθiː.ə.tə</font>/, /<font color="gray">ˈθɪə.tə</font>/, /<font color="gray">ˈθɪə.tɚ</font>/, /<font color="gray">θiˈeɪ.tə</font>/, /<font color="gray">θiˈɛt.ə</font>/, /<font color="gray">[ˈθiə̯tɜ]</font>/, /<font color="gray">[ˈθiə̯ɾɜ]</font>/<br>
